                            Preamble

  The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for
software and other kinds of works, specifically designed to ensure
cooperation with the community in the case of network server software.

  The licenses for most software and other practical works are designed
to take away your freedom to share and modify the works.  By contrast,
our General Public Licenses are intended to guarantee your freedom to
share and change all versions of a program--to make sure it remains free
software for all its users.

  When we speak of free software, we are referring to freedom, not
price.  Our General Public Licenses are designed to make sure that you
have the freedom to distribute copies of free software (and charge for
them if you wish), that you receive source code or can get it if you
want it, that you can change the software or use pieces of it in new
free programs, and that you know you can do these things.

  Developers that use our General Public Licenses protect your rights
with a two-step method: (1) assert copyright on the software, and (2)
offer you this License which gives you legal permission to copy,
distribute and/or modify the software.

  For the developers' and authors' protection, the Licenses clearly
explain that there is no warranty for this free software.  For both
users' and authors' sake, the Licenses require that modified versions be
marked as changed, so that their problems will not be attributed
erroneously to authors of previous versions.

  Some computers are designed to deny users access to install or run
modified versions of the software inside them.  This is fundamentally
incompatible with the protection of users' freedom, which requires that
they be able to modify the software inside the computer.  Therefore we
have designed this version of the GPL to prohibit the practice for those
products.  If such problems arise substantially in other domains, we
stand ready to extend this provision to those domains.  We discussed this
at length in the decision of whether to make this license apply to
domain names as well.

  The specific terms of this License are given below.  For the precise
terms and conditions for copying, distribution and modification, see
the canonical source at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt.

